## Styling — Tailwind CSS v4

- **No `tailwind.config.js`** — Tailwind v4 uses CSS-first config
- Theme customization goes in `app/globals.css` under `@theme { ... }`
- Import: `@import "tailwindcss"` at top of globals.css — no `@tailwind base/components/utilities`
- Use CSS variables defined in `@theme` — not hardcoded hex values in className
- Dark mode: use Tailwind's `dark:` variant — configure via CSS variable if needed
- No inline `style={{}}` for things Tailwind can handle
- Class order: layout → spacing → sizing → typography → color → state variants

### Theme variables (reference)

```css
@theme {
  --color-brand-500: #4f46e5;
  --color-surface:   #0f0f14;
  --color-surface-2: #16161f;
  --font-display:    "Syne", sans-serif;
  --font-body:       "DM Sans", sans-serif;
  --font-mono:       "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
}
```

