## Error Handling

- Server Actions return typed error states — never throw to the client
- Route handlers: always catch and return structured JSON errors
- Never expose stack traces or internal error messages to the client
- Log errors server-side with `console.error('[module] message:', err)`
- Use `satisfies` on error return types to ensure discriminated unions are exhaustive

---

## Security

- Validate EVERY input with Zod — no exceptions
- Never trust `req.headers` or `formData` without parsing
- Tenant isolation: every DB query MUST filter by `tenantId` from session — never trust client-provided tenantId
- Stripe webhooks: always verify `stripe.webhooks.constructEvent()` signature
- QStash webhooks: always verify signature before processing
- No secrets in client components — only in Server Components and Server Actions
